# {{ .Name }}

Snowflake project.

## Setup
{{- if .HasDevContainer }}

The project ships a devcontainer (`.devcontainer/`). Open it in an editor that
supports the Dev Containers spec, or start the stack yourself:

```sh
make devcontainer.up
make devcontainer.shell
```

The dev tools are installed inside the container by `postCreateCommand`; run
`make tools.install` manually if you started the stack by hand. Inside the
container the services are reachable by their compose service names
({{ if .HasDatabaseService }}`{{ if eq .Database.String "postgres" }}db{{ else if eq .Database.String "mysql" }}mysql{{ else }}mariadb{{ end }}`{{ if .HasKeyValueStore }}, {{ end }}{{ end }}{{ if .HasKeyValueStore }}`{{ .KeyValueStore.String }}`{{ end }}) rather than `localhost`; the compose
file sets the matching env vars, which take precedence over `.env`.

To work on the host instead, the service ports are published to `localhost`,
which is what `.env` points at:

```sh
make tools.install
```
{{- else }}

```sh
make tools.install
```
{{- end }}

Note: Be sure to check the docs of each tools.

## Commands

**Project-wide:**
- `make audit` - Code quality checks
- `make tidy` - Format and tidy code
- `make tools.install` - Install required tools
- `make tools.check` - Check if required tools are installed

**App:**
- `make run` - Run the app
- `make dev` - Run with hot reload (air)
- `make build` - Build the app
- `make test` - Run tests
{{- if .Templ }}
- `make templ` - Generate templ files
{{- end }}
{{- if ne .Database.String "none" }}
- `make sqlc` - Generate sqlc code
- `make db` - Show migration status
- `make db.up` - Run database migrations
- `make db.down` - Rollback last migration
- `make db.reset` - Reset and re-run all migrations
{{- end }}
{{- if .HasDevContainer }}
- `make devcontainer.up` - Start the devcontainer stack
- `make devcontainer.down` - Stop the devcontainer stack (removes volumes)
- `make devcontainer.logs` - Tail devcontainer logs
- `make devcontainer.shell` - Open a shell inside the dev container
- `make devcontainer.rebuild` - Recreate the devcontainer stack
{{- end }}
- `make docker.build` - Build Docker image
- `make docker.run` - Run Docker container
